<section class="disclaimer-box" aria-labelledby="bakersfield-actions-heading" id="apply-or-check-status">
	<h2 id="bakersfield-actions-heading">Bakersfield solar permit application and status</h2>
	<p>Confirm that the City of Bakersfield handles your property before using these links. A Bakersfield mailing address alone does not establish the permit jurisdiction.</p>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>Starting a residential solar application?</strong> The <a href={cityPortal} data-track-click="official_source_clicked">City's current application instructions</a> say to create a Clariti customer account before accessing Symbium for residential solar. That City page links to Clariti and embeds the Symbium application tool.</li>
		<li><strong>Looking for an existing permit?</strong> The City's <a href={permitSearch} data-track-click="official_source_clicked">Click2Gov permit search</a> offers searches by application number, address or parcel number. If your application is not there, ask the <a href={buildingDivision} data-track-click="official_source_clicked">Building Division</a> which system holds it before starting another application.</li>
		<li><strong>Ready for an inspection?</strong> The <a href={cityPortal} data-track-click="official_source_clicked">City's application and status page</a> also provides Clariti inspection instructions. Confirm the next inspection required for your permit with the City.</li>
	</ol>
	<p>These links do not establish your project's eligibility, current fee or approval time. Confirm those with the City; the older PV Toolkit facts below have their own source dates. PG&amp;E interconnection and permission to operate remain separate.</p>
	<p>To organize the local permit and utility steps, use the free <a href="/permit-path/" data-track-click="internal_resource_clicked">solar permit path checker</a>.</p>
	<p><small>Application links checked November 6, 2026. GridPermit is an independent guide and does not submit or approve permits.</small></p>
